NNAAMMEE
     mmkkuubboooott — create U-Boot files

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     mmkkuubboooott [--aa _a_r_c_h] [--ee _e_n_t_r_y] [--ll _l_o_a_d_a_d_d_r] [--nn _n_a_m_e] [--oo _o_s] [--tt _t_y_p_e]
             _i_n_f_i_l_e _o_u_t_f_i_l_e

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The mmkkuubboooott utility creates images suitable for loading using the U-Boot
     bootloader.

     The options are as follows:

     --aa _a_r_c_h      Sets the image architecture to _a_r_c_h.  For a list of valid
                  arguments, see below.

     --ee _e_n_t_r_y     Sets the entry point to _e_n_t_r_y.

     --ll _l_o_a_d_a_d_d_r  Sets the load address to _l_o_a_d_a_d_d_r.

     --nn _n_a_m_e      Sets the name of the loaded object inside the generated im‐
                  age.

     --oo _o_s        Sets the image OS to _o_s.  _o_s can be either “Linux” or
                  “OpenBSD”.

     --tt _t_y_p_e      Sets the type of the object to be loaded.  For a list of
                  valid arguments, see below.

     The following arguments are valid as the _a_r_c_h parameter:
           aarch64
           alpha
           amd64
           arm
           i386
           m68k
           mips
           mips64
           powerpc
           sparc
           sparc64
           superh

     The following arguments are valid as the _t_y_p_e parameter:
           standalone
           kernel
           script

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     An mmkkuubboooott utility first appeared in OpenBSD 4.4 as mmkkbboooott.

